 "seconds": 16.6,
 "text": "- **Q1 – B (electron affinity):** This is the energy change when an electron is added to a neutral gaseous atom.\n- **Q2 – C (1/√2):** cot⁻¹3 = tan⁻¹(1/3), and tan⁻¹(1/2) + tan⁻¹(1/3) = π/4, so sin(π/4) = 1/√2.\n- **Q3 – D (3.06 g):**\n  - Charge Q = 2.5 A × 1800 s = 4500 C, which is 0.0466 mol of electrons.\n  - Au³⁺ needs 3 electrons per atom, so 0.0155 mol of Au is deposited.\n  - 0.0155 mol × 197 g/mol ≈ 3.06 g.\n- **Q4 – A (Reinhard Genzel):** He shared the 2020 Physics Nobel.\n- **Q5 – C:** Hydrolith (CaH₂) is used to make hydrogen in portable generators.\n- **Q6 – C (falls):** Mercury does not wet glass, so it drops inside a capillary tube.\n- **Q7 – B (6):** Furan is aromatic with 6 delocalized π electrons.\n- **Q8 – A:** \"সভ্যতার সংকট\" is Rabindranath Tagore's essay.\n- **Q9 – C:** The metabolic nucleus is seen in interphase.\n- **Q10 – A (1969):** The economics Nobel was first awarded in 1969.\n- **Q11 – A:** Satire and ridicule (ব্যঙ্গবিদ্রূপ) distinguish a farce from a drama.\n- **Q12 – C (−266°C):** Lead becomes superconducting at about 7.2 K, which is roughly −266°C.\n- **Q13 – B:** In p², the 2 is a superscript, so the tag is `<sup>`.\n- **Q14 – B (9:7):** Duplicate recessive epistasis gives a 9:7 ratio.\n- **Q15 – A:** The usual adsorption order is –COOH > –OH > –NH₂ > –CHO; I am less certain of this one than the others.\n\n{\"answers\": {\"b38253e1-6890-442a-b951-96068e9d8b84-143692\": \"B\", \"b3b12d2a-6144-4e63-9cd4-f2dcfaf9634b-43867\": \"C\", \"b3e22892-3afb-4fde-a58f-621cc2b4ed0a-137362\": \"D\", \"b4d09688-21d6-4bca-9b5f-90230b1281c9-19616\": \"A\", \"b76637b1-ac57-4517-acb9-b393f55567c8-86394\": \"C\", \"b7c16856-e69a-46a4-b730-e75cd3a57d7e-28235\": \"C\", \"b911c06f-8b3a-49c3-8ae5-b1c81d2b27ab-56566\": \"B\", \"b935c5f8-8023-45af-a6ff-b42de66f722e-76058\": \"A\", \"b9a55ce7-cd40-44e8-bd86-e9247c2e3cda-143393\": \"C\", \"baf737d2-079d-47b5-a982-30aba341d89f-120791\": \"A\", \"bcc40a34-1744-4c94-ba13-ad3879bf63ea-43626\": \"A\", \"